    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second independent assessor.",
        "does_not_claim: That a near-unit dispersion correlation validates the nonlinear field against an electron micrograph.",
        "does_not_claim: That adult abdominal stripes or ommatidia have wavelength 2.736 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the spot lattice is a photograph of an ocellus.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Explicit-Euler periodic integration, radial-FFT wavelength, and eigenvector growth-rate correlation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gamma = 1.032078 is solved so argmax sigma(k) = 2 pi / 2.736 per micrometre.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mauritiana (a=0.16, b=0.72, Du=0.055, Dv=1.15) and miranda (a=0.07, b=1.25, Du=0.020, Dv=2.20) wavelengths at that shared gamma.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Registration of the steady activator onto the photograph at amplitude 0.16.",
        "reported_in_source: Richards et al. (2005) compare the D. pseudoobscura genome with D. melanogaster.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics are f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: The Karwath photograph is an adult male D. melanogaster under CC BY-SA 2.5.",
        "reported_in_source: True et al. (1997) quantify morphological divergence of D. mauritiana from the simulans complex.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavelength by diffusion-driven instability.",
        "reported_in_source: Wittkopp, True and Carroll (2002) place Drosophila melanin via Yellow and Ebony.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.736 µm is the assigned detail scale for this slot, not a published melanin-granule spacing.",
        "transfer_boundary: Chronospecies wavelengths are reconstructions. True 1997 and Richards 2005 do not report these micrometre values.",
        "transfer_boundary: Richards 2005 sequenced D. pseudoobscura. D. miranda is in that obscura clade; the paper is not a miranda pigment micrograph." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila melanogaster" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
